npm run dev (Local Development): Run this once in a dedicated terminal window whenever you are coding on your local machine. Leave it running in the background so it instantly recompiles your Tailwind CSS and JavaScript as you save files.

You only need to run npm run build once when you are ready to deploy your site to a live production server.

Since you are coding locally, you can ignore npm run build for now and just keep npm run dev running in the background while you work

Core Development Servers

php artisan serve — Starts the local PHP development server (usually at [http://127.0.0.1:8000](http://127.0.0.1:8000)). Run this in one terminal window to view your site.

php artisan serve --port=8080

npm run dev — Starts the Vite development server to compile Tailwind CSS and JavaScript in real-time. Keep this running alongside artisan serve while coding locally.

npm run build — Bundles, compresses, and compiles all CSS and JS assets into static files. Run this once when deploying your project to a live production server.

Database & Migrations

php artisan migrate — Executes any new, pending database migration files to update your tables.

php artisan migrate:fresh — Drops all existing database tables and re-runs every migration from scratch to reset your database schema.

php artisan migrate:fresh --seed — Wipes the database, re-runs all migrations, and populates initial data using your database seeders.

Caching & Troubleshooting

php artisan view:clear — Clears compiled Blade template cache. Essential when layout changes or view updates fail to render properly.

php artisan cache:clear — Clears the application's overall data cache.

php artisan config:clear — Clears cached configuration settings so recent changes in .env or config files take effect.

php artisan route:list — Displays a complete, structured table of all registered web routes, HTTP methods, URLs, and assigned controller actions.

Code Generation

php artisan make:model Post -m — Generates a new Eloquent model (Post) along with its corresponding database migration file in a single command.

php artisan make:controller Admin/PostController — Generates a new controller class inside a specific folder or namespace.